{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Power up",
  "description": "An old bridge console is switched on. 0 ms: a contactor slams in (steel on steel). 20 ms: the degauss coil shudders, a 100 Hz buzz that shakes hard and dies away over 600 ms. From 80 ms the cooling fan spins up from standstill to speed, straining at first. From 500 ms the logic comes alive: a stutter of start-up self-test glitches that clears as it stabilises. At 1.35 s the system is up and says so with a soft, slightly detuned open fifth that fades into the fan noise.",
